hadiths[52]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2875","Narrated Abu Hurairah:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent an expedition force [comprised] of many"""""
"2876","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Do not turn your houses into graves. Indeed Ash-Shaitan does not enter the house in which Surat Al-Baqarah is recited"""""
"2877","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): \For everything there is a hump (pinnacle) and the hump (pinnacle) of the Qur'an is Surat Al-Baqarah"""""
"2878","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever recites Ha Mim Al-Mu'min - up to - To Him is the return (40:1-3) and Ayat Al-Kursi when he reaches (gets up in) the morning"""""
"2879","Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin Abi Laila:that Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari had a store house in which he kept dates. A ghoul would come and take from it"
"2880","Narrated Abu Mas'ud Al-Ansari:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever recites the last two Ayat of Surat Al-Baqarah during the night"""""
"2881","Narrated An-Nu'man bin Bashir:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Indeed Allah wrote in a book two thousand years before He created the heavens and the earth"""""
"2882","Narrated An-Nawwas bin Sam'an:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \The Qur'an shall come"""""
"2883","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud:\Allah has not created in the heavens nor in the earth what is more magnificent than Ayat Al-Kursi.\"" Sufyan said: \""Because Ayat Al-Kursi is the Speech of Allah"""""
"2884","Narrated Abu Ishaq:hearing Al-Bara say: \There was a man reciting [Surat] Al-Kahf when he saw his riding animal stamping his feet"""""
"2885","Narrated Abu Ad-Darda:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever recites three Ayat from the beginning of Al-Kahf he is protected from the turmoil of the Dajjal"""""
"2886","Narrated Anas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed for everything there is a heart"""""
"2887","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever recites Ha Mim Ad-Dukhan during the night"""""
"2888","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever recites Ha Mum Ad-Dukhan during Friday night"""""
"2889","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\One of the companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) pitched a tent on a grave without knowing that it was a grave. Suddenly he heard a person from the grave reciting Surah al-Mulk till he completed it. So he went to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: 'Oh Messenger of Allah"""""
"2890","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Indeed there is a Surah in the Qur'an of thirty Ayat"""""
"2891","Narrated Jabir:The Prophet (ﷺ) would not sleep until he recited Alif Lam Mim Tanzil and: Tabarak Alladhi Biyadihil-Mulk.\ This Hadith was reported similarly by more than one from Laith bin Abi Sulaim. Mughirah bin Muslim reported it from Abu Az-Zubair"""""
"2892","Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever recites Idha Zulzilat"""""
"2893","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Idha Zulzilat is equal to half of the Qur'an"""""
"2894","Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to a man among his Companions: \Have you married O so-and-so?\"" He said: \""No by Allah O Messenger of Allah! And I do not have anything to marry with.\"" He said: \""Do you not know: Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad?\"" He said: \""Of course.\"" He said: \""It is a third of the Qur'an.\"" He said: \""Do you not know Idha Ja Nasrullahi Wal-Fath?\"" He said: \""Of course.\"" He said: \""It is a fourth of the Qur'an.\"" He said: \""Do you not know Qul Ya Ayyuhal-Kafirun?\"" He said: \""Of course.\"" He said: \""It is a fourth of the Qur'an.\"" He said: \""Do you not know Idha Zulzilat Al-Ard?\"" He said: \""Of course.\"" He said: \""It is a fourth of the Qur'an.\"" He said: \""Marry"""""
"2895","Narrated Abu Ayyub:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Would one of you like to recite a third of the Qur'an during a night? Whoever recited: Allaahu Al-Wahid As-Samad then he has recited a third of the Qur'an"""""
"2896","Narrated Abu Hurairah:\I went out with the Messenger of Allah and heard a man reciting Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad [Allahus-Samad] so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'It is obligatory.' I said: 'What is obligatory?' He said: 'Paradise"""""
"2897","Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever recited Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad two hundred times everyday"""""
"2898","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad is equal to a third of the Qur'an"""""
"2899","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Gather and I shall recite to you one third of the Qur'an.\"" He said: \""So whoever was to gather did so"""""
"2900","Narrated Anas bin Malik:\There was a man from the Ansar who led them (in Salat) at Masjid Quba. Every time he was to recite a Surah for them during Salat"""""
"2901","Narrated 'Uqbah bin 'Amir Al-Juhani:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Some Ayat have been revealed to me the likes of which have not been seen: Qul A'udhu Birabbin-Nas until the end of the Surah and Qul A'udhu Birabbil-Falaq until the end of the Surah"""""
"2902","Narrated 'Uqbah bin 'Amir:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered me to recite Al-Mu'awwidhatain at the end of every Salat"""""
"2903","Narrated 'Aishah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The one who recites the Qur'an and he is proficient with it"""""
"2904","Narrated 'Ali bin Abi Talib:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever recites the Qur'an and memorizes it"""""
"2905","Narrated Al-Harith Al-A'war:\I passed by the Masjid when the people were absorbed in story-telling. So I entered upon 'Ali and said: 'O Commander of the believers! Do you not see the people are becoming engrossed in story-telling?' He said: 'They have been consumed with it?' I said: \""Yes.' He said: 'As for me"""""
"2906","Narrated Abu 'Abdur-Rahman:from 'Uthman bin 'Affan that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The best of you is he who learns the Qur'an and teaches it.\"" Abu 'Abdur-Rahman said: \""So that is why I sit at this seat of mine.\"" And he taught the Qur'an during the time of 'Uthman until Al-Hajjaj bin Yusuf came. (Sahih)"""""
"2907","Narrated 'Uthman [bin 'Affan]:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The best of you - or the most virtuous of you - is he who learns the Qur'an and teaches it"""""
"2908","Narrated 'Ali bin Abi Talib:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The best of you is he who learns the Qur'an and teaches it"""""
"2909","Narrated Muhammad bin Ka'b Al-Qurazi:\I heard 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud saying: 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""[Whoever recites a letter] from Allah's Book"""""
"2910","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī al-Shawārib, narrated to us Abū ʿAwānah, narrated to us Abū ʿUthmān, a shaykh of his, from Anas رضي الله عنه that the Prophet ﷺ said to him: \O my little son.\""\n\nIn this chapter there are narrations from al-Mughīrah and ʿUmar ibn Abī Salamah رضي الله عنهما.\n\nAbū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīh gharīb hadith from this chain. It has also been narrated through other chains from Anas رضي الله"""""
"2911","Narrated Jubair bin Nufair:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \You shall not return to Allah with what is more virtuous than what came from Him.\"" Meaning the Qur'an"""""
"2912","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed"""""
"2913","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Amr:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \It shall be said - meaning to the one who memorized the Qur'an - 'Recite"""""
"2914","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \The one who memorized the Qur'an shall come on the Day of Judgement and (the reward for reciting the Qur'an) says: 'O Lord! Decorate him.\"" So he is donned with a crown of nobility. Then it says: \""O Lord! Give him more!' So he is donned with a suit of nobility. Then it says: \""O Lord! Be pleased with him.' So He is pleased with him and says: \""Recite and rise up"""""
"2915","Narrated Al-Muttalib bin 'Abullah bin Hantab:from Anas bin Malik that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The rewards for my Ummah were displayed before me"""""
"2916","Narrated Al-Hasan:that 'Imran bin Husain passed by a reciter reciting then he began begging. So he ('Imran) said: 'Indeed we are from Allah and to Him shall we return.' Then he said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: 'Whoever recites the Qur'an"
"2917","Narrated Suhaib:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \He does not believe in the Qur'an who makes lawful what it prohibits"""""
"2918","Narrated 'Uqbah bin 'Amir:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The one who recites the Qur'an aloud is like the one who gives charity publicly"""""
"2919","Narrated 'Aishah:\The Prophet (ﷺ) would not sleep until he recited Surat Bani Isra'il and Az-Zumar"""""
"2920","Narrated 'Irbad bin Sariyah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) would recite the Musabbihat (Chapters 17"
"2921","Narrated Ma'qil bin Yasar:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever says three times when he gets up in the morning: 'A'udhu Billahis-Sami Al-'Alim Min Ash-Shaitanir-Rajim' and he recites three Ayat from the end of Surah Al-Hashr - Allah appoints seventy-thousand angels who say Salat upon him until the evening. If he dies on that day"""""
"2922","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar, narrated to us Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan, narrated to us Fitr ibn Khalifah, narrated to me Mundhir, ath-Thawri, from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him), that he said: \O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"","" what do you think if a child is born to me after you"","" may I name him Muhammad and give him your kunya?\"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Yes.\"" He (Ali) said: \""So it was a concession (permission) for me.\"" This is a sahih hadith."""""
"2923","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Abi Qais [A man from Al-Basrah]:\I asked 'Aishah about the Witr of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"""""
"2924","Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah:\During the Mawqif (hajj season)"""""
"2925","Narrated Aisha (may Allah be pleased with she): The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) would set up a pulpit for Hassan in the mosque, upon which he would stand and boast on behalf of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) — or he said, \defend the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him).\"" And the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) would say: \""Indeed"","" Allah supports Hassan with the Holy Spirit (Ruh al-Qudus) as long as he boasts or defends the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him).\"""""""
"2926","Narrated Ibn Abi Mulaikah:that Umm Salamah said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would separate recitation reciting: 'Al-Hamdulillahi Rabbil-'Alamin' then he would stop. 'Ar-Rahmanir-Rahim' then he would stop. And he would recite it: 'Maliki Yawmid-Din"""""
